# VocalWriter 2.0.1's data files are in this repository, so that a clone runs.
# They are KAE Labs' software, 2005, not ours and not under our licence -- see
# NOTICE. Four of them are what the program needs:
#
#   assets/EnglishLex                            the dictionary
#   assets/GMSpeech.rsrc                         the voices
#   assets/GMBank.rsrc                           the wavetables the voices
#                                                with instrument names are
#                                                built on
#   assets/VocalWriter.app/.../VocalWriter.rsrc  the engine's tables
#   assets/VocalWriter.app/.../MacOS/VocalWriter the PowerPC binary, which the
#                                                interpreter and the C engine's
#                                                differential tests read
#
# The rest of the application -- the demo songs, the manual, the tutorial, the
# instrument bank -- is not needed to run it and is not here.
assets/*
!assets/EnglishLex
!assets/GMBank.rsrc
!assets/GMSpeech.rsrc
!assets/License Agreement.rtf
!assets/VocalWriter.app/
assets/VocalWriter.app/*
!assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/
assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/*
!assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/MacOS/
assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/MacOS/*
!assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/MacOS/VocalWriter
!assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/Resources/
assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/Resources/*
!assets/VocalWriter.app/Contents/Resources/VocalWriter.rsrc

# Their manual, which says in as many words that it may not be redistributed.
docs/manual.txt

# Audio rendered by VocalWriter itself, kept as the ground truth everything is
# measured against. It is their program's output, and 39 MB of it.
emu/out/

# What this program makes
out/
*.wav
*.aiff
*.vws

# What the build makes
build/
dist/
lib/
*.egg-info/

# Built, not written. The compiled core is made by `python -m ppc.build_core`
# for whichever interpreter will run it, and one built for CPython is no use
# to PyPy or to another platform.
*.pyd
*.so
*.dylib
# cffi writes this one beside the core it builds
ppc/_ppccore.c
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Environments and editors
.venv/
venv/
env/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The DECtalk source archives, unpacked. What is kept is the source: the C,
# the headers, the makefiles and project files, the scripts, the phoneme and
# dictionary tables, the notes. What is dropped is everything a compiler made
# and everything too big to belong in a git repository -- object files and
# libraries, precompiled headers and browse databases, executables and DLLs,
# the .svn pristine copies that duplicate every source file beside it, and the
# inner zips, PostScript and PDF that came along for the ride. They are still
# on disk in the working copy; they are simply not ours to publish and not
# worth 4 GB of history.
DECtalk source code archive/*.zip
DECtalk source code archive/**/.svn/
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.obj
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.o
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.a
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.lib
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.pch
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.sbr
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.bsc
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.exe
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.dll
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.dylib
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.so
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.pdb
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.ilk
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.idb
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.ncb
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.dep
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.cod
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.res
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.aps
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.plg
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.opt
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.tlb
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.ocx
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.msi
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.sys
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.drv
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.vxd
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.zip
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.tar
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.cab
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.ps
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.pdf
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.doc
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.docx
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.hlp
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.wav
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.au
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.aiff
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.gif
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.bmp
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.ico
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.png
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.jpg
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.jpeg
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.tif
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.mov
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.avi
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.bin
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.img
DECtalk source code archive/**/*.iso

# Claude Code. Session state, settings, worktrees and per-user memory live
# here, and they are one person's notes about their own work rather than
# anything about the program. Two people's sessions writing the same files
# would clobber each other's, so none of it is shared.
**/*claude*
**/*Claude*
**/*CLAUDE*
.claude/
.claude.json
.claude.json.backup
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# The plugin's build, and JUCE, which is 111 MB of someone else's repository
# and is cloned by vst/build_plugin.ps1 on the first build.
vst/build/
vst/libs/
vst/build_out.txt
